      },
      "verified_layout_inventory": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1898",
          "source_sha256": "8757eb0be7987dc447f4f325802c2c7d80db7fd489acc2950ffdccf6ec949360",
          "images_tables_mathml": 0,
          "literal_flattened_fragments": [
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[4]",
              "text": "The idea of a connexion between Europe & America, (whether quite continuous, or partially interrupted,) in high latitudes, seems rather supported than negatived by botanical facts.3 True, a good many plants of N.W. Europe are unknown in America; & vice versa. But (as a mere surmise, not investigated) if we could reduce the Ural chain to a few islands (like Iceland, Faroe &c.), & wash away much of the land on both sides, we should have a parallel case: diag 1 2 3"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[7]",
              "text": "Europe islands Asiaramme"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[9]",
              "text": "Forbes was not under the trammels of a very strict Conscience. He would be more likely to find “facts” to suit a conjecture, than those calculated to test its soundness. I should deem any one unwise who adapted his theories to Forbes’s statements of facts, unless those facts were verified afresh, or corroborated by others of like nature.4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1994",
          "source_sha256": "4d7369dd8dc114599c4ca42d2db9538a54b30cd28c18061a0fe1bae875d5795d",
          "images_tables_mathml": 0,
          "literal_flattened_fragments": [
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[5]",
              "text": "I have run over the last, 4th., edition & get these results.— diag Species by Numerals 1428"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[11]",
              "text": "Actual Number 1543ramme"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[15]",
              "text": "You will better see what I would convey by the alternative description, ‘treated expressly as varieties or not distinguished from near species’, if you will turn up the genus Ranunculus, in the first column of the Catalogue. Less than a century ago, all the species above Ficaria were held two only:— diag R. aquatilis."
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[16]",
              "text": "R. hederaceus.ramme From the first of these, many years ago, were separated diag R. circinatus."
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[17]",
              "text": "R. fluitans.ramme Opinions being much divided & long wavering, whether these two latter should be held species or varieties. The great majority, but not yet all botanical systematists, now admit them as species. Dr J. D. Hooker apparently holds them varieties."
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[18]",
              "text": "A few years ago, two others were separated from R. hederaceus:— diag R. tripartitus."
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[19]",
              "text": "R. cœnosus.ramme The former of these two is seemingly very local, & may not have ever been noticed apart from hederaceus (or even aquatilis, for it stands between) in England, until taken up as a species, & identified with a Continental one.— But R. cœnosus is widely & plentifully spread through England, & must have been often & constantly seen, & passed by as R. hederaceus, scarcely a variety, less than 20 years ago."
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[22]",
              "text": "I believe such instances as this may be found; the dates fanciful for the moment:— diag 1700 a. species"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[23]",
              "text": "1111 b. species"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[25]",
              "text": "1111 b. variety"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[28]",
              "text": "1111 b. variety"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[30]",
              "text": "1111 b. species.ramme"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2023",
          "source_sha256": "d463b763e00d6ffe8eabf3ed5a86c8bf445f43683b228f472b9cfb65164ea0fe",
          "images_tables_mathml": 0,
          "literal_flattened_fragments": [
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[31]",
              "text": "More briefly put it may be said that the following intermediate subspecies &c. are more rare than the species. diag Geum intermedium (Ehrh)"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[43]",
              "text": "A doubtful species between J. effusus and J. glaucus in general characters.ramme"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2183",
          "source_sha256": "919a3d242adc88edfdf2d2eca0f25e8234728ea2cb85b6a96cdae3cbdaa76ca0",
          "images_tables_mathml": 0,
          "literal_flattened_fragments": [
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[5]",
              "text": "Thus, Polygonum amphibium diag α natans"
            },
            {
              "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[6]",
              "text": "β terrestreramme are two states of a species, which no botanist would have united into one species, if they had arrived in England from 2 different countries. They are not in your list, just because they are known to be varieties from situation;—the very fact you want to reach thus causing their exclusion."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
